# tasks_objlist_placement: SetObjectAndPlacementList (68), which needs the argument-buffer feature, is accepted in every setup. Every validation the list's setter makes: offset + length overflow, a list or placement list ending at the task's end, a placement list shorter than 16 bytes an entry, and the alignment check (a misaligned offset is accepted, and the call after it is refused for it; the refusal zeroes the offsets, so the next call passes). Placement offsets are stored only with argument buffers, so a misaligned placement list matters only in the service. A placement list moved to new pages is copied there (min of both lengths); one over a read-only page cannot be mapped, "Unable to do placement list copy". Each result shows in the task root.
